title: Authorizations › Case page › A case at another site
route: /authorizations/case/I-2207
intro: What a case page does with the viewer's sites. A case at a site the viewer cannot see shows a short card that names the site and no patient. A viewer who can see both sites gets a quiet site label on the header and a Site fact.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the site of a case is fixed by the demo (the case ID decides; a denial belongs to the case it came from). Try it: Demo menu › 'Viewing as' › Dr. Rivera, then open /authorizations/case/I-2207 (a Site B case). A fresh load starts as Jordan Perez on Both sites.
---
start s1 "Open /authorizations/case/ID\n(a link, a notification, a row, or typed)"
process r0 "The page finds the request for the ID\nA denial's number is traced back to its case"
decision d0 "Is there a request for this ID?"
screen nf "'Request not found'\nNothing about any request is shown, so there is nothing to hide"
decision d1 "Is the case at a site in view?"
screen oos "Card: 'This case is not available at Site A'\n'I-2207 belongs to Site B. Dr. Rivera can see Site A only. Access follows the site so staff see only the patients they work with.'\nNo patient, no tabs, no numbers"
decision d2 "Can the viewer see both sites, and is one site selected in the top bar?"
click sb "Click 'Show both sites'"
store sc "The view becomes Both sites"
click bd "Click 'Back to the Dashboard' on the card"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Arrive › What the page shows"
endx e1 "The card stays\nThe viewer's role does not include that site, so there is no way past it"
screen cp "The case page opens as usual\nNext action, facts, tabs, History"
decision d3 "Can the viewer see both sites?"
screen lb "Quiet site label at the end of the sub line\n'J.M., 34 · Summit Medicaid HMO · Residential 3.5 · 14 days requested · Site A'\nand a 'Site' fact: 'Site A' with 'Main campus'"
screen nl "No site label and no 'Site' fact\n(a viewer with one site learns nothing from it)"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Ways in"

s1 --> r0 --> d0
d0 -->|No| nf
d0 -->|Yes| d1
d1 -->|No| oos --> d2
d1 -->|Yes| cp --> d3
d2 -->|Yes| sb --> sc --> cp
d2 -->|No| e1
oos --> bd --> g1
d3 -->|Yes| lb
d3 -->|No| nl
cp -.-> g2
